# B9 Subrogation — the 48-hour escalation, and the Graphite flag reader.
#
# THE HOST CLOCK IS UTC. Botswana is UTC+2, so subtract 2 from any Gaborone
# time you want here. The commands themselves do all their arithmetic in
# timezone-aware Django time (TIME_ZONE=Africa/Gaborone), so the schedule below
# only decides WHEN they look, never what they measure.
#
# 1. ingest_subrogation_flags — 06:40 UTC = 08:40 Gaborone, twenty-five minutes
#    after the nightly Graphite feed lands at 08:15 Gaborone. Idempotent: the
#    feed re-sends the whole snapshot every night and an already-flagged claim
#    is left alone, so it neither re-alerts nor restarts the 48-hour clock.
#    It is a quiet no-op until TheRiskCo starts sending the dataset.
#
# 2. subrogation_escalation_check — hourly on the half hour, weekdays. Hourly,
#    not daily, so a case that passes 48 hours at 10:00 is escalated at 10:30
#    rather than the following morning. It fires once per case for ever
#    (escalated_at), so running it 24 times a day cannot nag anybody twice.
SHELL=/bin/bash
PATH=/usr/local/sbin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/sbin:/usr/bin:/sbin:/bin

40 6 * * * root cd /opt/alpha-finance && /usr/bin/docker compose --env-file /etc/alpha-finance/.env exec -T backend python manage.py ingest_subrogation_flags >> /var/log/alpha-finance/subrogation-escalation.log 2>&1
30 * * * 1-5 root cd /opt/alpha-finance && /usr/bin/docker compose --env-file /etc/alpha-finance/.env exec -T backend python manage.py subrogation_escalation_check >> /var/log/alpha-finance/subrogation-escalation.log 2>&1
